{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794425451,"nonce":"VBsctwY4UQRxheszJC9LcnYMBE8=","title":"Reported 2026-11-12 from the devops-gitops pilot on Scarab 0.3.2. Read from the code at v0.3.2; not run on the cluster.","message":"A `build:` step cannot pass build arguments. `BuildSpec` (crates/scarab-pipeline/src/lib.rs:1508) has only `context`, `dockerfile`, `image` and `push`, and is `deny_unknown_fields`, so `args:` is a parse error.\n\nProposed:\n\n    build:\n      args:\n        VERSION: \"1.4.2\"\n        GIT_SHA: ${{ event.sha }}\n\n-\u003e `--opt build-arg:VERSION=1.4.2 --opt build-arg:GIT_SHA=\u003csha\u003e`.\n\n- Keys: `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*`, checked at compile time.\n- Values follow the rule a `command` element follows today (ADR-0076, 2026-10-30 amendment): literals, plus outside values only of a fixed shape (`event.sha`, `event.number`, `event.kind`, …, `crates/scarab-pipeline/src/event.rs` `FIXED`), each rechecked when the Step launches. A build arg ends up in image history and in `RUN` shells, so free-text event fields (branch names, titles) must not reach it.\n- Rendering: today `build.*` is not rendered at all (see the ticket on `build.image` and `${{ }}`); this needs the same renderer.\n\nDecide first whether build options stay in core (see the ticket \"build: should image building leave core\"). If `build` becomes a library, `args` is a library input.\n\nWorkaround today: same as the cache ticket, a `privileged` grant (ADR-0039) for a digest-pinned BuildKit image in an Environment, with buildctl run by hand.\n\nAcceptance: `args:` compiles, reaches buildctl as `--opt build-arg:K=V`, a free-text event field in a value is refused with a diagnostic, and a Dockerfile `ARG` sees the value.","files":null}]}